# Q10 – Documentation formats for requirements in ML-enabled systems (least-used two)

Script: `analysis.py` (executed; pandas 3.0.2, numpy, scipy). Random seed 20261022, 10,000 bootstrap replicates.
Outputs: `out/q10_results_primary_n194.csv`, `out/q10_sensitivity_all_bases.csv`,
`out/q10_excluded_categories.csv`, `out/q10_target_comparison.csv`, `out/boot_replicates_primary.npy`.

## 1. Input
`data/requirements_engineering_for_ML-enabled_systems.csv` → 276 respondents x 202 columns (277 file lines = header + 276).

## 2. Sentinel / value audit (levels actually present in the 12 coded Q10 columns)
Only three raw levels exist in every coded Q10 column: `quoted`, `not quoted`, `-77`.
There is **no ordinal scale** ("Not Used at All" … ) and no "I don't know" option in Q10 of this file.

| raw value | meaning | handling |
|---|---|---|
| `quoted` | respondent indicated this format | 1 = used |
| `not quoted` | respondent saw the item and did **not** indicate it | 0 = valid answer, "not used" |
| `-77` | block/item never shown (82 rows, all `Status = Suspended (22)`, all 12 coded columns simultaneously) | NA → excluded from the primary denominator; in the n=276 sensitivity base it can never count as "used" (0 in numerator) |
| `-99` | no answer / not applicable (57 other columns of the file; 179 in `Others_Free`) | NA, never "used" |
| `-66` | placeholder in free-text columns (43 columns; 82 in `Others_Free`) | NA, never "used" |

Confirmed: -77 / -99 / -66 are treated as NA and never as an indication of use; `not quoted` IS a valid
response. No Q10 value outside the three levels above occurs (checked programmatically).

## 3. Denominators (multi-select question)
primary n=194 (saw the Q10 block) | n=276 all rows | n=164 documenting (did not check Not_Documented) |
n=140 documenting with >=1 named format | n=188 = 194 minus the 6 `Suspended` respondents that did see Q10.

