## 5. Robustness of the ranking
Rank order is **identical in all five bases** (194 / 276 / 164 / 140 / 188): rank 1 = BDD_Scenarios,
rank 2 = MLCanvas, rank 3 = Vision_Document = Goal_Models (tie), … rank 10 = Notebooks. Only the absolute
percentages move with the denominator. Removing the 6 Suspended respondents that answered Q10 (n=188) leaves
the ranking untouched and moves CIs by <0.5 pp (MLCanvas 7.979% [4.255, 12.234]; BDD 2.128% [0.532, 4.255]).

## 6. Comparison with the published targets
| target | assigned format | % at n=194 | abs gap (pp) | target inside exact CI? | % at n=140 | abs gap (pp) |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 10.13% [9.926, 10.333] | MLCanvas (2nd least used) | 7.732 | 2.40 | yes | **10.000** | **0.13** |
| 4.366% [4.231, 4.501] | BDD_Scenarios (least used) | 2.062 | 2.30 | yes | 2.857 | 1.51 |

* Under the primary base both published point estimates fall inside our exact 95% CIs (bootstrap two-sided
  p = 0.221 and 0.041; the bootstrap grid is coarse for k=4, which the exact CI handles properly).
* Under the "documenting with >=1 format" base MLCanvas lands at 10.000% — 0.13 pp from the published 10.13%.
* Relative order is the decisive evidence: the larger published value (10.13%) must map to the 2nd least used
  format (MLCanvas) and the smaller one (4.366%) to the least used (BDD_Scenarios). No other pair of named
  formats is below 14% in any base.

## 7. Limitations of the reference values (not of this calculation)
* The published CIs are far too narrow for this sample: [9.926, 10.333] implies SE ≈ 0.104 pp → effective
  n ≈ 84,448; [4.231, 4.501] implies SE ≈ 0.069 pp → n ≈ 88,009. With n=194 the binomial SE at 10% / 4%
  would be 2.15 pp / 1.41 pp. So the reference CIs cannot be reproduced from 276/194 rows — they come from a
  different sample size/weighting (probably the full published survey release).
* Count-ratio mismatch: observed MLCanvas/BDD = 15/4 = 3.75 vs published 10.13/4.366 = 2.32.
* Percentages were NOT tuned to match the targets; observed values are reported as computed.

## 8. Data caveats found during QC
* 6 respondents checked `Not_Documented` **and** at least one named format (indices 37, 61, 114, 118, 128, 134),
  one of them MLCanvas — hence MLCanvas is 15/194 but 14/164 and 14/140. Inconsistent multi-select answers were
  kept (they are valid rows); this is why the primary base does not filter on Not_Documented.
* `Others` free text: 1 usable text was blank (1 NaN) though `Others = quoted`.

## 9. Answer
The two least-used documentation formats are **ML Canvas — 10.13% — and BDD scenarios — 4.366%**.
